  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rLocation Plan\rBlock Plan 001\r00.100\r01.100\r01.101\r201\r202\r203\r204\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that match the existing building or as specified in the approved application.\r\rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 2015, or any amending Order, no external windows or doors other than those indicated on the approved drawings shall be installed in the development hereby approved without the approval in writing of the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To safeguard the privacy of the occupiers of adjoining properties.\r",
    "The proposed extensions to Nos. 91 and 93 New River Crescent as demonstrated on Drawing Nos. 00.100, 01.101, 202, and 204, hereby approved shall be carried out as one joint development and the approved extensions to either property shall not be erected except in conjunction and simultaneously with the extension to the other property, and shall not be completed in full independently of each other.\r\rReason: In the interests of the residential amenities of the occupants of the properties.\r\r"
  ]
